  "content": {
    "title": "Leonardo DiCaprio keeps it classic at 2026 Oscars red carpet – See photos",
    "text": "March 15, 2026, 7:58 p.m. ETWhen it comes to the red carpet, Leonardo DiCaprio always keeps it classic.The actor, 51, stepped onto the red carpet at the 2026 Oscars in a black tuxedo with a white shirt. DiCaprio accessorized his look with a Rolex watch and a bee pin on the collar of his tux. The star of the look was his chevron mustache.DiCaprio is in the running for best actor for Paul Thomas Anderson's \"One Battle After Another\" alongside Michael B. Jordan (\"Sinners\"), Timothée Chalamet (\"Marty Supreme\"), Wagner Moura (\"The Secret Agent\"), and Ethan Hawke (\"Blue Moon\").In \"One Battle,\" DiCaprio ditches his Hollywood leading man image for a ratty red robe, unkempt hair and oversized sunglasses as former revolutionary and current stoner Bob Ferguson, who is forced back into action to save himself and his daughter (Chase Infiniti) from paramilitary enforcers.USA TODAY Style Meter: Vote for the best looks at the Oscars!The Paul Thomas Anderson film is also in the running for the night's biggest prize – best picture. See photos of Leonardo DiCaprio at the 2026 Academy AwardsDiCaprio last won a best-actor Oscar in 2016 for \"The Revenant.\" 2026 would truly be the new 2016 if DiCaprio snags an award tonight.Contributing: Bryan Alexander / USA TODAYSaman Shafiq is a trending news reporter for USA TODAY. Reach her at sshafiq@usatodayco.com and follow her on X and Instagram @saman_shafiq7.",
